~ start
do Global.is_autoplay = true
do Global.play_voice("button")
Narrator: Great! And there's the button. Go ahead and press it.
Narrator: You did well enough, [wait=1.0] but keep in mind that you won't always be able to teleport just anywhere.
Narrator: If you're standing in an empty field in one world, [wait=1.0] there might be a meatpacking plant in that exact same spot in another.
=> END

~ desert_entered
do Global.is_autoplay = true
do Global.play_voice("desert_entered")
Narrator: ... Looks like we can't get through here.
Narrator: I think you know what to do.
Tip: [wave]You can travel in different dimensions to overcome some obstacles[/wave]
=> END


~ valley_entered
do Global.play_voice("valley")
do Global.is_autoplay = true
do Global.input_locked = true
Narrator: What's that saying they have on Stavrapulon? [speed=0.8][i]Ten teeth are better than two![/i][/speed]
Narrator: ...I suppose you've hardly heard that proverb.[wait=1.0] Considering... you were born just a couple of minutes ago.
Narrator: Anyway, try entering that door at the end of the stone path.[wait=3.0] That's a stable [color=green]Ind Soc[/color] phase transporter,[wait=1.0] for civilian use!
Narrator: Unfortunately [wait=0.5] due to the tear in the fabric of space-time on this planet, [wait=1.0]all doors lead to god-knows-where.
Narrator: But I don't think we have any other options anyway.[wait=2.0] You can't climb the cliffs.[wait=1.0] You don't have hands!
do Global.input_locked = false
=> END
